WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:54.300
<b>Water Seven, 22 Years Ago</b>

3
00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:59.390
<b>The Legendary Shipwright</b>

4
00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.410
Hey! What in the hell
is wrong with you!

5
00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.180
Ow!

6
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.350
Idiot! Don't you know
you're not supposed to

7
00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.490
be goofin' around right now?

8
00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.150
<b>Iceburg
16 Years Old</b>

9
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.260
We got real ships to work on, not your
crappy toys!

10
00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.960
Don't yell at me when
you don't have a clue

11
00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.030
what you're talkin'
about, ice-for-brains!

12
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.650
<b>Cutty Flam (Franky)
12 Years Old</b>

13
00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.600
It isn't some crappy toy,
it's my super battleship,

14
00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.570
The Battle Franky!

15
00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.970
[ICEBURG]
Whatever it is, you
need to leave it alone

16
00:03:00.010 --> 00:03:01.030
before someone gets hurt!

17
00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.930
This is Scrap Heap Island!
I can do what I want!

18
00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.240
Wait! You'll see.

19
00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.240
I'm gonna build a
battleship awesome enough

20
00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:08.300
to take down a sea king!

21
00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.040
Bull! What you're gonna
do is get yourself killed!

22
00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:11.940
Oh yeah?

23
00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:12.610
Yeah! Quick!

24
00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:13.440
Nu-uh!

25
00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.580
Real quick!

26
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.220
[TOM]
If you wanna be a man, show some gusto!

27
00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:46.750
<b>President Tom (Longhorn Cowfish Fishman)
Tom's Workers Shipbuilding</b>

28
00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.380
Well there's the ol'
launching ceremony.

29
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:48.010
One more ship sailing
with gusto! Right, buddy?

30
00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:48.960
<b>Yokozuna (Sumo Frog)
Tom's Pet</b>

31
00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.540
Erp! Erp! Erp!

32
00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.940
That's about enough work for today.

33
00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.780
Whaddaya say
we head on home?

34
00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.080
Erp! Erp!

35
00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:59.680
<b>Opposite the Warehouse Under the Bridge
Water Seven</b>

36
00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.860
Man, I'm hungry!

37
00:03:56.890 --> 00:03:57.590
Erp! Erp!

38
00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.060
Let's see what's for dinner!

39
00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.570
Erp! Erp!

40
00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.810
<b>Scrap Island
(Tom's Workers Dockyard)</b>

41
00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:04.010
[ICEBURG]
Hey, hold on! Wait for us!

42
00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:15.160
[TOM]
So today's Battle Franky model
was number-what-are-you-up to?

43
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.690
[FRANKY]
Eight sir! It was
really beautiful!

44
00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.820
No it wasn't!

45
00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.090
Your dumb weapon that he
let you build for some reason

46
00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.520
fell apart after you almost
killed both of us with it!

47
00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.660
Nobody asked you, ya
stupid Ice-for-brains!

48
00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:29.320
Ice-for-brains?
Well you're Flunky!

49
00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.080
Alright. That's enough
fighting, boys. Cut it out.

50
00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.100
[BOTH]
– He started it. Not me!
– He started it. Not me!

51
00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.140
[TOM laughing]

52
00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:44.560
<b>Kokoro, a Beautiful Secretary
Tom's Workers</b>

53
00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.640
My word. Don't
encourage those two, Tom.

54
00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.100
Was it that funny?

55
00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.410
Keep laughing and
they'll keep misbehaving.

56
00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.640
Speaking of misbehaving.

57
00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.210
I heard that another
ship carrying lumber

58
00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:51.380
was attacked by pirates.

59
00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:54.650
I swear, ever since the King
of the Pirates was executed

60
00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:58.180
this place has just gone rotten
with those no-good bums.

61
00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:00.090
They're taking over the city.

62
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.120
The people's spirits are really low.

63
00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:12.920
"Merchant"

64
00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:05.160
And because of all the
flooding from Aqua Laguna,

65
00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.990
we can only get lumber and iron

66
00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.600
if we ship them in
from other islands.

67
00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:11.200
But with all the storms
and pirates everywhere,

68
00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:13.070
it's near impossible.

69
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.970
The shipyards are starting to
get so desperate for customers,

70
00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.600
they are literally fighting
each other for them.

71
00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.200
So many have closed down already.

72
00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:24.800
At this rate, Water Seven is on
a course to sink into the ocean,

73
00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:26.630
and fade from
the world's memory.

74
00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.730
And to think, this
city made its name

75
00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.470
making unforgettable,
unsinkable ships. Such a shame.

76
00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.300
Hey, you built a big,
super-awesome pirate ship once,

77
00:05:35.340 --> 00:05:36.710
now didn't ya Tom?

78
00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:39.680
Will ya teach me how to
draw up blueprints for one, too?

79
00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.650
What's so funny, huh?

80
00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:49.150
[TOM]
Franky, there's no such thing as
blueprints for a pirate ship.

81
00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:53.490
It's the flag, boy. Skull
and bones means pirate ship.

82
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.620
And a seagull flag means that it's Navy.

83
00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.270
Whatever you build
just remember this.

84
00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:04.710
Build it with pride and a
whole lot of manly gusto!

85
00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.120
[FRANKY]
You sure are working late
tonight. What're ya drawin'?

86
00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:17.220
[TOM]
This here. Is hope
for our island.

87
00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.460
It is?

88
00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:21.500
Yep. Well at least,
that's what I'm hoping

89
00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:25.530
that it'll turn into someday.
Now, to bed with ya.

90
00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.030
[FRANKY]
Yes, sir.

91
00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:37.090
[seagulls crying]

92
00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:47.100
Huh? Whoa!

93
00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:49.400
[MAN]
The Judicial Ship is here!

94
00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.340
What the heck is that?

95
00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:54.540
A mobile court. I wonder
who they're here for.

96
00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.010
[FRANKY]
Whaddaya think you're doing?

97
00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.680
Let him go ya big stupid jerk!
He didn't do anything wrong.

98
00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:08.140
Don't you worry.
I'll be just fine!

99
00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:15.650
No Tom! Come back!

100
00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.600
[MARINE]
Justice was brought
to Gold Roger,

101
00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.340
The King of the Pirates,
by way of execution!

102
00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:29.780
His ship, the Oro Jackson, was
built by none other than Tom,

103
00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.450
who stands before
this court today!

104
00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:34.550
As penalty for aiding and
abetting that vicious criminal,

105
00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:36.580
Tom will be taken
to Enies Lobby,

106
00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.890
where he will be executed!

107
00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:40.280
No!

108
00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:45.320
[MAN]
The verdict was read! Guilty!
They're gonna execute Tom!

109
00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:46.420
They say it's

110
00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:48.820
because he built a ship
for the King of the Pirates.

111
00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:49.990
Damn shame.

112
00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:53.490
That thing brought a whole lot of grief
into the world.

113
00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:55.490
Now, building ships is not a crime.

114
00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.560
And one may sell them to almost anyone who
wishes to buy.

115
00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:02.070
But we must make an exception for the King
of the Pirates.

116
00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:04.240
On the charge of providing
meaningful assistance

117
00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:07.110
to the man who
terrorized the entire world.

118
00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:11.460
We hereby sentence Tom
to death. Take him away!

119
00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:13.300
Come on, time to go.

120
00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.210
Move it! You heard him!

121
00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.230
Hurry up!

122
00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.130
Go already!

123
00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.010
[MARINE]
Hey, what're you doing?!

124
00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:20.060
[TOM]
I've got a new design.

125
00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:23.550
For a completely new
kind of paddle steamer!

126
00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:27.950
A train that will run on the
surface of the ocean with gusto!

127
00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:30.150
[MARINE]
Shut up and get movin'!

128
00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.590
[TOM]
This once great island has lost its gusto.

129
00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:38.030
Our trade is not what is used
to be. People have lost hope.

130
00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:40.930
Water Seven is slowly sinking away.

131
00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:44.600
Every day our hard working
citizens are filled with worry.

132
00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.940
I can lift their spirits.

133
00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:51.840
I will by building our
good people a sea train!

134
00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.850
[commotion among PEOPLE]

135
00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.050
[MARINE]
Quit flappin' your gums
and move your feet.

136
00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:57.410
[JUDGE]
No, let him stay.

137
00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.360
[MARINES]
– Huh?
– Huh?

138
00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.300
Sea train. Tell me more.

139
00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:02.380
It's like a ship.

140
00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:06.190
But one that puffs out steam and runs on a
track.

141
00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.940
It'll go between the islands,

142
00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:10.040
carrying people and
all kinds of goods.

143
00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.540
Even other ships.

144
00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:15.360
Most importantly, it won't be affected by
conditions at sea.

145
00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.000
[MAN]
That's ridiculous!

146
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:19.230
A railway on the water
will be ripped to pieces

147
00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.570
once Aqua Laguna comes around.

148
00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:21.730
And even if it doesn't,

149
00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.530
what're ya gonna do about
all the Sea Kings out there?

150
00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.530
[TOM]
It doesn't have to be a completely fixed
track.

151
00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:29.970
It'll be submerged
under the water a bit,

152
00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:32.290
so it won't be
bombarded by the waves.

153
00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:34.960
It'll sway just like
a rope in the water.

154
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.860
The sea train will
just use the tracks

155
00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.230
as a guide to get
from place to place.

156
00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.370
I'm also considering
installing a mechanism that

157
00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:45.170
emits a loud dissonant sound
underwater to discourage fish

158
00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.970
from getting anywhere
near the tracks.

159
00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.090
It should work on
Sea Kings as well,

160
00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:50.260
so they won't pose a threat.

161
00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.700
Whoa, is all that possible?

162
00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:57.140
If we connect St. Poplar, Pucci,
San Faldo and this island.

163
00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:01.110
We can create a booming economy
that will help out all of us.

164
00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.180
[WOMAN]
Amazing!

165
00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.710
[TOM]
I will be finished with the blueprints
very soon.

166
00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.650
But it will take a master shipwright to
build it.

167
00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:10.520
Now could this sea train
run to Enies Lobby as well?

168
00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:12.750
Without a doubt, your honor.

169
00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.740
[MARINE gulping]

170
00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.940
Once the plans are in the can
and the railway is in the water.

171
00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.250
People can go with gusto
from island to island

172
00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.420
for work or play!

173
00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:26.470
And once again Water Seven
will be a city filled with hope!

174
00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:28.170
[JUDGE]
How long will it take?

175
00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.530
[TOM]
10 years.

176
00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.040
[JUDGE]
Then build it!

177
00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:33.370
If you agree to
develop this sea train,

178
00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:35.270
I will give you
the time to do it.

179
00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:38.480
Consider these next
ten years as probation!

180
00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.520
[PEOPLE cheering]

181
00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:41.550
[MAN]
That's great news!

182
00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.540
Good luck, Tom!

183
00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:46.190
Save Water Seven, please!

184
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.930
I'm glad you think this is so funny.

185
00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.200
I thought you were a goner.
I was worried sick over you.

186
00:10:57.230 --> 00:10:59.240
But I guess if this
plan of yours works out,

187
00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:00.150
they're willing to forgive

188
00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.190
and forget the whole
Gold Roger affair.

189
00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:05.190
Mwell! I just gotta tell ya
how amazed I am with ya Tom!

190
00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:07.320
What a great idea!
It's unbelievable!

191
00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.590
To think that you just came
up with that on your own!

192
00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.500
It's Brilliant! When you told...

193
00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.300
[FRANKY]
Thanks for the grub!
Come on, Yokozuna!

194
00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.460
I'll teach you the front crawl!

195
00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.600
Erp!

196
00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:18.230
Hey, we're all celebrating here and you
wanna leave?

197
00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.240
What's your deal?!

198
00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:22.440
My deal?! What happened
to Tom was so unfair!

199
00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.200
He built the only
ship that was able

200
00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:25.570
to sail the whole Grand Line!

201
00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.580
Something no one else
in the world could do.

202
00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:30.580
And those jerks wanna
put him to death over it?!

203
00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.220
They don't realize how hard that is!

204
00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:33.780
They couldn't even
string together a raft

205
00:11:33.820 --> 00:11:35.220
if their lives depended on it!

206
00:11:35.330 --> 00:11:37.460
I mean, I know that the
whole reason our office

207
00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.730
is under this bridge is
'cause those stupid people

208
00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:41.800
kicked you out of
town over that ship!

209
00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.540
You're the greatest
ship builder the world

210
00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.150
has ever known and they
treat you like garbage!

211
00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.590
What're ya laughin'
at ya big yellow weirdo?

212
00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:52.500
[ICEBURG]
You're crazy! Stop attacking
him, ya stupid kid!

213
00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:55.340
[FRANKY]
Why does he have ta
laugh at everything?

214
00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.630
[splashing]

215
00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:00.580
No, no, no!
You're doin it wrong!

216
00:12:00.770 --> 00:12:04.740
Stroke harder and push that water back!

217
00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.180
Erp! Erp!

218
00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:10.140
No! No! Do it harder!
Don't hold back!

219
00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:11.550
That Franky's got a lotta nerve.

220
00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.320
If I were you, I'd kick him out for what
he just did!

221
00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.390
Mwell, I know the boy
can be a handful,

222
00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.860
but he's a fellow shipbuilder.

223
00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:19.090
At his young age,

224
00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:22.290
he's almost on par with the
best craftsmen on the island.

225
00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:25.330
He does build battleships, yeah.

226
00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:28.300
His problem is he's too honest.

227
00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.800
[TOM]
Two years ago, I met that
kid on Scrap Heap Island.

228
00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:38.510
He'd gone there to collect
junk to make a cannon,

229
00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.940
and was firing it with gusto!

230
00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.980
Old guy hey! Help me out.

231
00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:45.750
My good-for-nothing parents ditched me!

232
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:47.420
Apparently, his folks
couldn't handle

233
00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:48.820
his rambunctious behavior,

234
00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.790
so they threw
him off their ship.

235
00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:53.690
Sounds like a couple of heartless pirates
to me, eh?

236
00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.160
What a joke.

237
00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.420
Now, Tom.

238
00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.460
He is one tough kid.

239
00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:02.500
He's had a rough go at it, but he's still
got a good heart.

240
00:13:02.530 --> 00:13:05.070
I'm positive that both of
you boys are gonna grow up

241
00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:07.470
to be world-class
shipwrights some day.

242
00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.040
There's no need for you to be rivals.

243
00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.840
I don't know about all that.

244
00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.180
It's like he's allergic to sanity or
something.

245
00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:16.160
Mwell. I just need to
finish those blueprints

246
00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.130
and then we'll build
ourselves a sea train!

247
00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:21.790
[ICEBURG]
Yeah. I bet he
won't help at all.

248
00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:24.080
[TOM]
He can do whatever he wants!

249
00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:02.840
[MAN]
Suicide?

250
00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.110
That's the word. Head of
the fourth largest shipyard.

251
00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.760
What a tragic story.

252
00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.960
They ran out of materials
so he took a ship out

253
00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:15.220
to sea to get some more.
Lost fifty men on the water.

254
00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:18.090
They had to close down his shop.

255
00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:21.160
Aw man. Will this
be how it ends?

256
00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:24.660
Is this how Water Seven finally dies?

257
00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:30.600
Hey! Did you guys hear?
Big news from Scrap Heap Island!

258
00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.150
No way! Did they do it?!

259
00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:37.020
Did Tom's Workers actually
finish the sea train?!

260
00:15:37.050 --> 00:15:40.220
Whoa! Is this crazy
thing really gonna work?

261
00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:42.990
I don't know if I trust something built by
a criminal.

262
00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:43.910
[WOMAN]
I'll try it out!

263
00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.430
[MAN]
What the heck, me too!

264
00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:47.270
They gonna tell us
how it works?!

265
00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.800
All aboard ladies and gentlemen!

266
00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:54.090
[train whistle]

267
00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:57.610
There it goes!

268
00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:02.300
The paddles are grabbing the railway!

269
00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:05.230
[GIRL]
Man that is the
coolest thing ever!

270
00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:18.780
[NARRATOR]
Twelve years ago,
departing from an isolated city

271
00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.880
in decline and full of

272
00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:24.750
passengers who'd almost given
up hope for a brighter future.

273
00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:29.490
[train whistle]

274
00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.690
The sea train
"Puffing Tom" embarked

275
00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:35.090
on its maiden voyage
across the sea!

276
00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.190
Interesting.

277
00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.060
[LUCCI]
Many ships were born
in this cobwebbed room

278
00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:51.630
and now look at it. Filthy.

279
00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.700
[USOPP]
They built ships here?

280
00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:59.340
[LUCCI]
Tom, Iceburg, and Cutty Flam.

281
00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:01.540
This place must hold
countless memories of days

282
00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.700
when you still shared
a life with those two.

283
00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:08.480
And now you call it
"your top secret base."

284
00:17:08.510 --> 00:17:10.970
That's heartbreakingly adorable.

285
00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:15.210
[FRANKY]
Damn you. Just get
the hell out already!

286
00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:18.250
[LUCCI]
We won't leave till we get what we're
after.

287
00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.000
Make this easy on yourself.

288
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:22.980
[FRANKY]
There ain't no blueprints in here!

289
00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:26.240
[LUCCI]
Oh? No? You don't say?

290
00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.190
[FRANKY]
Hey!

291
00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.230
[LUCCI]
Kalifa!

292
00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:37.770
Dammit!

293
00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:40.340
Just keep it together Usopp.

294
00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.720
[FRANKY groaning]

295
00:17:44.070 --> 00:17:45.740
[FRANKY]
You bastard.

296
00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:46.910
Take your time,

297
00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:49.880
but be aware that we know
many things about your past.

298
00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.720
Things that you don't want getting out.

299
00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:54.420
For example, we know what happened eight
years ago.

300
00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:55.450
And that you are guilty

301
00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.860
of committing a very
serious crime back then.

302
00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:00.460
Just like your dear old Tom.

303
00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:03.430
You shut up! Tom was
never a damn criminal!

304
00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:07.460
You don't know what the hell
you're talking about! You freak!

305
00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:12.090
Tom!

306
00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:22.540
[USOPP]
Stay back!

307
00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:25.510
[LUCCI]
I disagree.
You're both criminals.

308
00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:26.780
And as such,

309
00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:30.050
you should be made to feel the
consequences of your actions.

310
00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.380
[TOM]
Franky. Whatever happens,

311
00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:35.020
don't interfere with
what I'm about to do.

312
00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:37.150
No matter what.

313
00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:39.360
[FRANKY]
You talk like you know everything.

314
00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:42.260
You don't know Tom.

315
00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:47.200
And you don't know anything about Water
Seven!

316
00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.440
<b>Water Seven, 8 Years Ago</b>

317
00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:00.570
[WOMAN]
I heard the Judicial Ship
will be here in three days.

318
00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:03.140
[MAN]
Finally putting Tom on trial, are they?

319
00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.670
I hope it ends well for him.

320
00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:06.540
I'm sure it will.

321
00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.680
Right. He fulfilled
his promise after all.

322
00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:12.350
That he did.

323
00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:18.110
[WORKMAN]
Alright, let's get
that lumber in the dock!

324
00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:20.530
So, how'd the deal work out with St.
Poplar?

325
00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.530
Not that great.

326
00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.000
They're taking advantage of us

327
00:19:23.030 --> 00:19:25.500
since we don't have
much to trade with 'em.

328
00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.450
Like iron from San Faldo.

329
00:19:27.510 --> 00:19:30.580
We'll all be in the red if
this kinda crap keeps up!

330
00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.620
We're not gonna let this keep
happenin', now are we guys?!

331
00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:36.690
[WORKMEN]
– Yeah! No way!
– Yeah! No way!

332
00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:42.430
[ICEBURG]
The people do seem to be happy

333
00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:44.330
about being able
to cross the ocean.

334
00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:48.300
But they say the trade situation isn't as
good as they'd hoped.

335
00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:51.040
I wonder if this town needs more than a
sea train.

336
00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.360
Ah, but their
spirits are up, boy!

337
00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:58.500
That's a major step,
so give the rest some time.

338
00:19:58.530 --> 00:19:59.730
We've done our best,

339
00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:04.070
so be proud, keep your head
held high and walk with gusto!

340
00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.230
Yeah.

341
00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:10.080
[knocking]

342
00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:15.780
[SPANDAM]
You there!

343
00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:16.940
Am I correct in assuming

344
00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.250
I'm speaking with Mr. Tom,
the shipbuilding engineer?!

345
00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.350
You're a difficult man to pin down.

346
00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:25.420
I have some matter of
great importance I wish to...

347
00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:26.550
[ATTENDANT]
Uhm Sir?

348
00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.290
[SPANDAM]
This man and I are talking!

349
00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.020
[ATTENDANTS]
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

350
00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:31.320
[SPANDAM]
Again before I was so rudely...

351
00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:40.680
<b>Director-General Spandam
Cipher Pol Number 5</b>

352
00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:40.730
I was going to say.
My name is agent Spandam.

353
00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:43.200
From Cipher Pol Number Five!

354
00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.600
[ATTENDANTS]
– Spandam, sir!
– Spandam, sir!

355
00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:49.720
OW! Sorry about that! My bad!

356
00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:53.180
[FRANKY]
Looks like you got in the way
of my victory cannon salute!

357
00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:57.250
Tough luck! It's! Super!

358
00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:59.600
Battle Franky thirty-five
comes back home with booty!

359
00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:01.680
That's right. Check it out!

360
00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:06.220
Is this not the biggest Sea King
you ever laid your eyes on?!

361
00:21:07.690 --> 00:21:11.290
I can't believe him.
Still acting like a child.

362
00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:17.530
Hey! What hell do ya think
you're doing, Ice-for-brains?!

363
00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:19.200
Will you ever grow up?

364
00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.260
Ever since you were a kid

365
00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:22.420
all you wanna do is build
these stupid battleships!

366
00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.530
It's time to stop!
This better be the last one!

367
00:21:25.560 --> 00:21:28.330
Or I'm gonna start
tearin' em all apart myself!

368
00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:29.560
Wanna bet?!

369
00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.270
You lay a finger on my ship
and you'll draw back a stump!

370
00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:33.000
You hear me?!

371
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.260
Yeah? Mwell! Listen, Franky!

372
00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:37.200
If you were able
to kill a Sea King

373
00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.410
with this floating
piece of junk

374
00:21:38.440 --> 00:21:40.240
that means it's a
dangerous weapon.

375
00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.140
And you've got all
those other "battleships"

376
00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:43.470
of yours just
strewn around here?

377
00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:44.660
What're you thinking?!

378
00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:47.850
Hey, it's not like I'm attacking
people with them, am I?

379
00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:49.540
[ICEBURG]
I'm not saying you'd do that!

380
00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:50.710
But you're making it easier

381
00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:53.710
for anyone else who'd
want to, you idiot!

382
00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.630
Sir...

383
00:21:57.930 --> 00:22:00.370
Am I right? Back me up here Tom!

384
00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:03.400
Flunky's weapons are gonna
be the end of our business!

385
00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:06.940
Ah! "Flunky" That's rich!

386
00:22:06.950 --> 00:22:09.360
[SPANDAM]
Hold on! This is
no laughing matter!

387
00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.560
I demand a sincere apology!

388
00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:14.460
And that you listen to
what I've come here to say!

389
00:22:14.490 --> 00:22:18.500
Government guy are ya?
So, is this about the trial?

390
00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:20.870
Trial? What the devil
are you talking about?

391
00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:24.640
No, this concerns an altogether different
matter.

392
00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:30.270
[KOKORO]
Did Tom come back with you boys?

393
00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:32.210
[ICEBURG]
No, I think he's with a visitor.

394
00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.980
Some man from the government.
It wasn't about the trial.

395
00:22:36.010 --> 00:22:38.350
Span-Span something.

396
00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:40.320
[FRANKY]
Span-Something, dumb? Maybe?

397
00:22:40.350 --> 00:22:43.390
How strange. And he's not
from the judicial ship?

398
00:22:43.450 --> 00:22:46.350
The government is so disorganized.

399
00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:49.990
Fraid not.

400
00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:52.760
I've got no blueprints for something like
that.

401
00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:54.820
That's nonsense!

402
00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:57.460
Do you take me for some kind
of weak minded simpleton?!

403
00:22:57.490 --> 00:23:00.660
I researched the history of
Water Seven for countless hours!

404
00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:02.770
And I am absolutely
certain this document

405
00:23:02.800 --> 00:23:05.270
can only be in your possession!

406
00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:08.570
You're saying that
you actually have

407
00:23:08.600 --> 00:23:10.670
the authority to
investigate me?

408
00:23:10.810 --> 00:23:13.920
That's right, I do!
And what's more.

409
00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:16.650
I learned all about your
dealings with Gold Roger

410
00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:18.730
in the course of
my investigation.

411
00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:20.900
So unless you want me
to share that information

412
00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:22.590
with my colleagues,
you're going to cooperate.

413
00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:25.600
Why would I care? The government
already knows about it!

414
00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:28.410
We do? That's utter poppycock!

415
00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:29.680
If that's true,

416
00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:33.480
why are you here and not rotting
away somewhere in a jail cell?

417
00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:36.480
[TOM]
Use your investigative powers and find out
for yourself.

418
00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:37.540
Good day.

419
00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:40.980
[SPANDAM]
Hey! You can't treat a
government agent like this!

420
00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:43.320
Open the door this immediately!

421
00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:49.060
[SHOPKEEPER]
That's right.
It's all true. Yes sir.

422
00:23:49.090 --> 00:23:51.760
He did exactly what he told the judge he'd
do.

423
00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:53.830
And they should be dropping

424
00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:56.000
the charges at the
trial that's coming up.

425
00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:58.840
That man saved this island, for sure.

426
00:23:58.990 --> 00:24:00.140
[SPANDAM]
It makes my blood boil.

427
00:24:00.140 --> 00:24:04.880
To think, that damned criminal
is being treated like a hero.

428
00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:08.930
I see. You're certain that
such a thing truly exists?

429
00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:10.180
Yes sir!

430
00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:13.320
And the pirates are scouring the globe for
it as we speak.

431
00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:16.040
That's why it's imperative we locate it
immediately.

432
00:24:16.070 --> 00:24:18.310
If it were to fall
into the wrong hands,

433
00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:20.710
the resulting destruction
would be inconceivable.

434
00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:24.190
<b>The Five Elders</b>

435
00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:23.350
We've been suffering through
this "great pirate era"

436
00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:24.660
for more than a decade now.

437
00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:28.160
It's a vile sickness that grows worse with
every passing day.

438
00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:30.060
The time for idle discussion is over.

439
00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:32.860
We must do more than to prevent this
weapon's construction.

440
00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:34.130
We must build it ourselves

441
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:36.800
and use it as a mighty
instrument of justice!

442
00:24:36.830 --> 00:24:39.000
With it, we can eliminate
this pirate scourge

443
00:24:39.050 --> 00:24:41.820
and bring law and order
back to our land!

444
00:24:41.820 --> 00:24:43.450
[FIVE ELDERS]
Hmm.

445
00:24:43.490 --> 00:24:47.620
This is indeed a troubling era.
There's no doubt about that.

446
00:24:47.660 --> 00:24:49.690
Your primary objective
will be to locate

447
00:24:49.730 --> 00:24:51.290
and then obtain
these blueprints.

448
00:24:51.340 --> 00:24:53.410
That will be all at this time.

449
00:24:53.440 --> 00:24:56.950
We trust that you can complete this
mission, Spandam.

450
00:24:57.070 --> 00:24:59.370
[SPANDAM]
Yes sir! Without fail!

451
00:25:00.070 --> 00:25:02.610
I've been working on
this case for far too long

452
00:25:02.640 --> 00:25:04.020
to see it all go up in smoke.

453
00:25:04.020 --> 00:25:06.720
It's right within my grasp now.

454
00:25:10.740 --> 00:25:11.670
Let's go!

455
00:25:15.050 --> 00:25:18.520
Damn! If the judge
decides to acquit him

456
00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:20.980
that'll mean a
real headache for me.

457
00:25:21.020 --> 00:25:22.550
[ATTENDANTS]
– Spandam, sir!
– Spandam, sir!

458
00:25:28.560 --> 00:25:32.360
The charge will stick
and that bastard will hang.

459
00:25:32.390 --> 00:25:36.660
Men! I'll need five
more agents, stat!

460
00:25:42.470 --> 00:25:44.040
Spandam, sir!

461
00:25:47.210 --> 00:25:48.880
[TOM]
Iceburg, Franky.

462
00:25:48.880 --> 00:25:49.480
[FRANKY]
Yeah?

463
00:25:49.480 --> 00:25:50.880
[TOM]
Hey, boys, come here.

464
00:25:50.910 --> 00:25:52.010
What's up?

465
00:25:52.040 --> 00:25:55.080
It's about time I let you
in on somethin' important!

466
00:25:58.490 --> 00:26:01.960
Why would anyone even dream of something
like this?

467
00:26:02.460 --> 00:26:05.500
Is this for real? Can this
thing actually be built?

468
00:26:05.530 --> 00:26:09.170
Those are the blueprints for
a nightmare, a real monster.

469
00:26:09.200 --> 00:26:11.270
The government has
learned of their existence

470
00:26:11.300 --> 00:26:13.370
and has started
sniffing around for them.

471
00:26:13.530 --> 00:26:15.800
It's too dangerous for me to keep them
anymore.

472
00:26:16.330 --> 00:26:20.320
[ICEBURG]
This is terrifying,
but I agree. I'll keep them.

473
00:26:20.320 --> 00:26:25.090
Wow, Iceburg. Hey let's see
if we can build this thing!

474
00:26:25.100 --> 00:26:26.280
You idiot!

475
00:26:26.620 --> 00:26:28.720
Do you ever think
before you speak?!

476
00:26:30.320 --> 00:26:31.830
This thing can never be built.

477
00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:35.100
Do you realize how much destruction it
could cause?

478
00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:41.830
Yeah, the world
would be done for.

479
00:26:46.300 --> 00:26:48.300
Besides tryin' to
build the damn thing,

480
00:26:48.340 --> 00:26:50.370
you can do whatever the
hell you want with it for now.

481
00:26:50.400 --> 00:26:52.170
Even toss it if you need to.

482
00:26:52.210 --> 00:26:53.910
Yes, of course.

483
00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:58.550
[TOM]
While I got your attention.
Here's another storm a brewin'.
